config {
  type: "assertion",
  tags: ["tiktok", "monitoring"],
  description: "Each demographic cut must total the campaign report on its own. Since stg_tiktok_demographic dropped its QUALIFY on 2026-11-17 this is the ONLY guard left on the source: if the v2 tables ever start re-appending their window, it shows up here as exactly 2.0."
}

-- An assertion FAILS if it returns rows. Empty result = healthy.
--
-- WHY THIS CHECK AND NOT A GRAIN CHECK. A uniqueKey assertion on the fact
-- confirms the rows are unique, which they will be whatever the source
-- does, because staging groups on that key. It cannot tell whether the
-- right rows survived, or whether a day was counted twice.
--
-- Comparing the total against fct_tiktok_campaign_daily can. The two are
-- independent extractions of the same spend, so the ratio is the test.
--
-- THIS GOT MORE IMPORTANT ON 2026-11-17. Until then the source shipped
-- every row twice -- 30,596 rows for 15,331 age keys on 2026-11-11 -- and
-- stg_tiktok_demographic removed the copies with a largest-wins QUALIFY.
-- The model now reads tiktok_agev2 and titktok_genderv2, which hold one
-- row per key, and the QUALIFY is gone. Nothing downstream absorbs a
-- duplicate any more, so a source that starts re-appending arrives here
-- undisguised. Measured 2026-11-11 the ratio was exactly 2.0000 on every
-- closed day before de-duplication and 1.0000 after. So:
--
--   near 2.0   the v2 tables are re-appending their window -- check the
--              Load Type on the Keboola BigQuery writer, which was the
--              cause both previous times
--   near 0.5   a key is too coarse somewhere and real rows are being
--              discarded, which is what stg_meta_age_gender did for five
--              weeks
--   near 1.0   healthy
--
-- EACH breakdown_type IS CHECKED SEPARATELY, because each is a complete cut
-- of the campaign on its own. Checking them together would compare 2x the
-- campaign against 1x and fail forever.
--
-- TOLERANCE IS 2%. TikTok's demographic report and its campaign report are
-- separate extractions and the smallest buckets get suppressed, so exact
-- equality is not expected. The failures this guards against land at 2.0 or
-- 0.5, nowhere near the band.
--
-- THE LAST TWO DAYS ARE EXCLUDED. The Keboola feed lands at 09:48 UTC and
-- the Weld one at 00:06, so the newest days disagree by timing alone.

WITH demografic AS (
  SELECT
    date                      AS zi,
    breakdown_type            AS taietura,
    SUM(impressions)          AS impresii
  FROM ${ref("fct_tiktok_demographic_daily")}
  WHERE date < DATE_SUB(CURRENT_DATE(), INTERVAL 2 DAY)
  GROUP BY 1, 2
),

campanie AS (
  SELECT
    date                      AS zi,
    SUM(impressions)          AS impresii
  FROM ${ref("fct_tiktok_campaign_daily")}
  WHERE date >= (SELECT MIN(date) FROM ${ref("fct_tiktok_demographic_daily")})
    AND date < DATE_SUB(CURRENT_DATE(), INTERVAL 2 DAY)
  GROUP BY 1
)

SELECT
  d.zi,
  d.taietura,
  c.impresii                                        AS impresii_campanie,
  d.impresii                                        AS impresii_demografic,
  ROUND(SAFE_DIVIDE(d.impresii, c.impresii), 4)     AS raport,
  'fct_tiktok_demographic_daily no longer totals fct_tiktok_campaign_daily. A ratio near 2.0 means tiktok_agev2 or titktok_genderv2 started re-appending its extraction window -- check the Load Type on the Keboola BigQuery writer, it must be Full load. A ratio near 0.5 means a key is too coarse and is discarding real rows.' AS actiune
FROM demografic d
JOIN campanie c USING (zi)
WHERE c.impresii > 0
  AND ABS(d.impresii - c.impresii) > c.impresii * 0.02
